   "title": "Say hello",
   "text": "A visitor walks up to the Fox. Your program reads their name. Print a hello for them, like this: Hello, Ana!",
   "check": {
    "solved": true
   },
   "why": "((Text#py_read_line|read a line)) reads the next line of the <<input>>, and ((Text#text_join|join)) sticks pieces of text together. So “Hello, ” + the name + “!” makes the greeting.",
   "checklist": [
    {
     "text": "Put ((Text#text_print|print)) in the ((Events#py_program|Program)) block",
     "check": {
      "blocks": [
       "text_print"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "Read the name with ((Text#py_read_line|read a line))",
     "check": {
      "blocks": [
       "py_read_line"
      ]
     }
    },
    {
     "text": "Press [[Check my answer]]: every test passes",
     "check": {
      "solved": true
     }
    }
   ],
   "hints": [
    "Use ((Text#text_join|join)) to stick “Hello, ”, the name and “!” together, and <<print>> it.",
    "In ((Events#py_program|Program)): ((Text#text_print|print)) ((Text#text_join|join)) with three pieces: “Hello, ”, ((Text#py_read_line|read a line)) and “!”."
